#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c82bbc8-83bc-55f8-be32-4d63f6db7261" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9df07d21-c011-5a20-8d0d-50e29dca3cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186088951} {:answer/id #uuid "e31ac7fd-5e45-5605-84b7-bf45605d0074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186088952} {:answer/id #uuid "f0001a67-76a1-52d3-af7f-1b5fcf44d6bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186088953} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce39470-a260-5f16-8141-3c26af182a95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2} - \\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186088954} {:answer/id #uuid "744637ee-dfc5-5605-8bff-5b53b2087780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\pi } - \\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186088955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0001a67-76a1-52d3-af7f-1b5fcf44d6bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186088953} :answer-field/id #uuid "2526896e-69c2-5e03-8091-d740dc1e8ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186088950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "977bb89c-c84c-5262-ad82-39cc342b286c" :question/math-academy-id "q-10260" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059427/assets/5117030d23370b2167513b7a2eee5258aae4eb9f45ad428fd82e4334c4ce6638.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1+3t,\\,y=2{t}^{3/2},\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3/2})=3{t}^{1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{(3{t}^{1/2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9+9t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+t)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\\cdot {\\frac{2}{3}(1+t)^{3/2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{8}-2 \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebd2a5c8-5d15-589d-81c9-9b67f4e8f0b3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Parametric Curve Containing Special Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df23ba4c-322f-5fc7-b35c-62614b410f0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{5{sin}^{2}⁡t-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+32}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337673} {:answer/id #uuid "630de36d-f891-5720-994c-cd5ca01b5ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337674} {:answer/id #uuid "2c8dced7-0d7e-5362-8950-dd402b3b6dd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337675} {:answer/id #uuid "df6b4862-9700-52d8-9959-e7bfa365aadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{8{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+8}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337676} {:answer/id #uuid "57bc87d9-25f4-5fe2-a09d-9912b39de6bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{10{sin}^{2}⁡t-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57bc87d9-25f4-5fe2-a09d-9912b39de6bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{10{sin}^{2}⁡t-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337677} :answer-field/id #uuid "686fe979-0d5e-5bdb-975a-3702e1512152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a37e6009-e864-56bc-93ae-b166a2b05514" :question/math-academy-id "q-123027" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=8t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\nfrom $t=-1$ to $t=1$ ?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=8-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(8-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+64-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{10{sin}^{2}⁡t-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+64}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebd2a5c8-5d15-589d-81c9-9b67f4e8f0b3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Parametric Curve Containing Special Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d4ba437-3c22-5035-a06b-81a306e49bca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{3{sin}^{2}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337680} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d10aa3-f972-5374-98a9-aee16a124368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337681} {:answer/id #uuid "fac1f9cd-ec8f-532e-a5bf-d126e96ff060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337682} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e5fe5b-59f6-5247-b4f4-fe90049360ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337683} {:answer/id #uuid "8d619fca-f90d-5146-9be3-71804e5e68c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fac1f9cd-ec8f-532e-a5bf-d126e96ff060" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337682} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce576d09-0f0d-5640-9cbb-4e47252b3ef7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a2f2890-829e-5660-aa0e-71dea52c1f55" :question/math-academy-id "q-15178" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059427/assets/ca290e8fd51edddf4381ec267b8e0a5692d0e52bd2a36b7d43ab89cbeb5cf00d.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ (shown above)?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+4{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c82bbc8-83bc-55f8-be32-4d63f6db7261" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e54eefaf-5718-5727-b1e7-00b051a3a154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337687} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5203e7-295c-5cde-ade8-7bdc57017df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337688} {:answer/id #uuid "eb1279d0-877a-5f5a-9885-6f66c080cbe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337689} {:answer/id #uuid "f0c577fb-691d-57fd-ab02-f70a3a9b2a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337690} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4d8ca0-be6d-56ac-86ac-23faa6a962da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4d8ca0-be6d-56ac-86ac-23faa6a962da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337691} :answer-field/id #uuid "da5aa7ec-dabe-5539-bb7e-9025da25e2b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb9131cb-db34-55f4-9b8c-bfeb56041029" :question/math-academy-id "q-20907" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+5,\\,y=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1),\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+5))=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+16{sin}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c82bbc8-83bc-55f8-be32-4d63f6db7261" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Arc Length of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f21b4205-fe95-5d61-aa2e-072832d7192a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f21b4205-fe95-5d61-aa2e-072832d7192a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337694} :answer-field/id #uuid "42de287f-50e0-5642-9370-c74cd9501015" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49cd7d08-c239-5b6f-9d68-7ee1350ff2ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-348088" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059427/assets/be9e314ed11882842bbf9a74deeb3a994596c8275a4e854ffc66327fa0008058.png)\n\nFind the arc length $L$ of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ].\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$L=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{2}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =2{\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
